          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.4.5 Avoiding harmful substances — learn to say NO"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.473,
            0.744,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some people, including your peers, may tempt, persuade, force or, create pressure on you to consume harmful substances such as tobacco, gutka, cigarettes, beedi, alcohol, or even life-threatening illegal drugs. Since adolescence is marked by curiosity and excitement, adolescents might get influenced by such people and try these substances."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.585,
            0.744,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These substances are not just harmful to physical and mental health but are also addictive. This means that once people start consuming them, they develop a strong urge to take them again and again. Over time, they start using them regularly. This is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "substance abuse",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
